{
  "id": "29469_kokuin",
  "headword": "{刻印|こくいん}",
  "reading": "こくいん",
  "romaji": "kokuin",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "engraved mark; stamp; hallmark",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "engraved mark; stamp; hallmark; (to) engrave, imprint",
      "explanation": "A mark cut or pressed into a hard surface such as metal, leather, or a seal, often to show a maker, purity, or authenticity. As {刻印|こくいん}する it means to engrave or stamp such a mark, and figuratively to leave a lasting impression on the mind."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29469_kokuin_ex1",
      "japanese": "{指輪|ゆびわ}に{刻印|こくいん}がある。",
      "english": "There is an engraving on the ring.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29469_kokuin_ex2",
      "japanese": "{金|きん}の{純度|じゅんど}を{示|しめ}す{刻印|こくいん}が{押|お}されている。",
      "english": "A hallmark showing the purity of the gold has been stamped on it.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29469_kokuin_ex3",
      "japanese": "その{光景|こうけい}は{今|いま}も{記憶|きおく}に{刻印|こくいん}されている。",
      "english": "That scene is still etched into my memory.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Compound of {刻|こく} (to carve) + {印|いん} (mark, seal). Used both for a physical engraved mark and, with する, for the act of engraving or leaving a deep impression.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {刻印|こくいん}を{押|お}す: to apply a stamp/hallmark\n- {刻印|こくいん}を{入|い}れる: to add an engraving\n- {記憶|きおく}に{刻印|こくいん}される: to be etched into memory\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {刻印|こくいん}する: to engrave, to imprint — the verb use\n- {烙印|らくいん}: brand mark — burned in, often figurative as a stigma\n- {彫刻|ちょうこく}: sculpture, carving — three-dimensional carving rather than a mark",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
